  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Sleep mode
  </title>
  <p>
    Sleep mode temporarily disables Orca for an application. It can be activated manually or
    automatically for selected applications. The settings and commands below control when Orca
    enters sleep mode.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-sleep-mode">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Sleep mode</gui> category (global only).
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Always use sleep mode with these applications</gui>: Lists applications
          for which Orca automatically enters sleep mode. Add an application, then enable or
          disable automatic sleep mode for its entry. An application must be running to add it;
          saved applications remain listed even when they are not running.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-sleep-mode">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Sleep mode</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle sleep mode for the current application</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Alt</key>
            <key>Shift</key>
            <key>Q</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
        <p>
          Enters or leaves sleep mode for the current application. While Orca is asleep for an
          application, only this command remains available; use it again to wake Orca.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
